// One class per way a date can select rows: a product's reference data valid
// over business dates, an account whose status is recorded over processing
// time, an issuer's rating that is both, and trades that carry a plain date and
// a plain date-time and reach the first two through milestoned properties.

###Pure
Class <<temporal.businesstemporal>> demo::dates::Product
{
  id: Integer[1];
  name: String[1];
}

Class <<temporal.processingtemporal>> demo::dates::Account
{
  id: Integer[1];
  status: String[1];
}

Class <<temporal.bitemporal>> demo::dates::Rating
{
  issuer: String[1];
  grade: String[1];
}

Class demo::dates::Trade
{
  id: Integer[1];
  tradeDate: StrictDate[1];
  executedAt: DateTime[1];
  quantity: Integer[1];
  product: demo::dates::Product[0..1];
  account: demo::dates::Account[0..1];
}
